::ENG2_U05_L05_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Draft: "The library should stay open later. Students need it." Which revision best fits school leaders as the audience?{
=A. The library should remain open later because students who ride late buses need a supervised place to complete assignments.#Correct. This revision is clear, formal, and audience-aware.
~B. The library should stay open because it is cool.#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
~C. I want the library open because I like it.#Incorrect. This is too personal.
~D. Students need it and stuff.#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which feedback is actionable?{
~A. This is bad.#Incorrect. It does not explain what to fix.
=B. Add evidence showing why students need the library after school.#Correct. This identifies a specific revision action.
~C. Make it better.#Incorrect. This is too vague.
~D. I do not get it.#Incorrect. This may show confusion but does not specify revision.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is complete and correctly punctuated?{
~A. Because the library closes early.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~B. Students need a place to study, the library should stay open.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
=C. Because the library closes early, some students lose access to a quiet study space.#Correct. This sentence is complete and correctly punctuated.
~D. Students study library because quiet.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence gives the clearest expository explanation?{
~A. The library is good.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. It helps.#Incorrect. The pronoun is unclear and the explanation is weak.
~C. Students need things.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=D. The library provides computers, tables, and a quiet setting for students completing assignments after school.#Correct. This gives specific explanation.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Feedback: "Your tone is too casual for school leaders." Which revision best responds?{
=A. Extended library hours would support students who need a supervised study space after school.#Correct. This uses formal, audience-appropriate language.
~B. Keeping the library open would be awesome.#Incorrect. Awesome is too informal.
~C. The library thing should happen.#Incorrect. This is vague and casual.
~D. I really, really want this.#Incorrect. This is personal and informal.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q06::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which feedback should the writer probably not use?{
~A. Explain who would benefit from the revision.#Incorrect. This is useful feedback.
=B. Change the topic from library hours to favorite sports.#Correct. This feedback is off-task and does not improve the assigned draft.
~C. Add a clearer reason for the claim.#Incorrect. This is useful feedback.
~D. Replace vague wording with precise language.#Incorrect. This is useful feedback.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q07::[MLA.ENG2.W.02] Argument claim: "The library should stay open later." Which sentence best supports the claim?{
~A. Libraries have books.#Incorrect. This is general and weak.
~B. Some people like quiet places.#Incorrect. This is too broad.
=C. Students who ride late buses need a supervised place to complete assignments while they wait.#Correct. This supports the claim with a clear reason.
~D. School buildings have doors.#Incorrect. This is irrelevant.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q08::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best improves audience fit?{
~A. You should just do what I say.#Incorrect. This is demanding and inappropriate.
~B. The library is super useful.#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
~C. It should stay open because yeah.#Incorrect. This is informal.
=D. School leaders should consider extended library hours because students need a safe academic space after school.#Correct. This fits the audience and purpose.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q09::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence fixes the comma splice: "Students need a place to study, the library is quiet"?{
=A. Students need a place to study, and the library is quiet.#Correct. The coordinating conjunction correctly joins the complete thoughts.
~B. Students need a place to study, the library is quiet.#Incorrect. This keeps the comma splice.
~C. Students need a place to study the library is quiet.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
~D. Because the library quiet.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q10::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which sentence best explains a revision choice?{
~A. I changed it because I changed it.#Incorrect. This does not explain the revision.
=B. I added "supervised place to complete assignments" so school leaders understand the specific student need.#Correct. This explains how the revision helps the audience.
~C. I made it longer with extra words.#Incorrect. Length alone is not the goal.
~D. I removed the claim because feedback exists.#Incorrect. Feedback should improve the claim, not erase it automatically.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q11::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which phrase is most precise?{
~A. good place#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. helpful thing#Incorrect. This is vague.
=C. supervised study space#Correct. This phrase is specific and audience-appropriate.
~D. stuff for students#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q12::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] What is the first step when using feedback?{
~A. Delete the whole draft.#Incorrect. That is not usually the first step.
~B. Add random sentences.#Incorrect. Revision should be purposeful.
~C. Ignore the audience.#Incorrect. Audience matters.
=D. Identify what the feedback asks you to improve.#Correct. Writers must understand the feedback before revising.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q13::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which revision improves clarity and conventions?{
=A. Since some students wait for late buses, they need a quiet place to study after school.#Correct. This is clear and correctly punctuated.
~B. Since some students wait for late buses.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~C. Some students wait, late buses they need quiet.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~D. Students wait late buses, they need quiet.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice and unclear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q14::[MLA.ENG2.W.02] Which feedback best improves an argument?{
~A. Add more colors to the paragraph.#Incorrect. This does not improve argument writing.
=B. Add a reason that explains why the claim matters to students.#Correct. Arguments need support and reasoning.
~C. Use fewer complete sentences.#Incorrect. This would weaken clarity.
~D. Change the claim to an unrelated topic.#Incorrect. That does not improve the argument.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q15::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best responds to feedback asking for more audience awareness?{
~A. I think this is great.#Incorrect. This remains writer-centered.
~B. The library is nice.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=C. Extended library hours would help students who cannot leave campus until late buses arrive.#Correct. This explains the audience need.
~D. People should agree.#Incorrect. This does not address the audience.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q16::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence has the clearest voice for expository writing?{
~A. The thing is really good.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~B. I just like it a lot.#Incorrect. This is personal.
~C. It is awesome for everyone.#Incorrect. This is exaggerated.
=D. Extended library hours provide students with additional time and space to complete academic work.#Correct. This is clear and explanatory.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q17::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Feedback: "Your reason is unclear." Which revision is strongest?{
=A. Add a sentence explaining that students who ride late buses need a supervised place to work.#Correct. This directly responds to unclear reasoning.
~B. Add a joke to make it interesting.#Incorrect. This does not clarify the reason.
~C. Remove the topic sentence.#Incorrect. This would weaken the paragraph.
~D. Use more vague words.#Incorrect. This would make the reason less clear.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q18::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence has correct pronoun clarity?{
~A. When students asked teachers about the library, they said it should stay open.#Incorrect. "They" is unclear.
=B. When students asked teachers about the library, the students said it should stay open.#Correct. This clarifies who said the library should stay open.
~C. They asked them about it.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~D. The library asked students about teachers.#Incorrect. This is illogical.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q19::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision goal best matches audience needs?{
~A. Make every sentence complicated.#Incorrect. Complicated sentences may hurt clarity.
~B. Use slang so school leaders sound casual.#Incorrect. Slang does not fit the formal audience.
=C. Make the reason clear, specific, and respectful for school leaders.#Correct. This matches the audience and purpose.
~D. Remove all evidence.#Incorrect. Evidence supports the audience's understanding.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q20::[MLA.ENG2.W.02] Which sentence gives reasoning, not just evidence?{
~A. Some students ride late buses.#Incorrect. This is evidence or a fact, not reasoning.
~B. The library has tables.#Incorrect. This is a detail.
~C. The library closes at four.#Incorrect. This is a fact.
=D. Because students must wait after school, extended library hours would give them productive time to complete assignments.#Correct. This explains why the evidence supports the claim.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q21::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which feedback is vague?{
=A. Make this better.#Correct. It does not identify what needs revision.
~B. Add a specific example of how students use the library.#Incorrect. This is specific.
~C. Replace casual wording with formal language.#Incorrect. This is actionable.
~D. Correct the comma splice in sentence two.#Incorrect. This is specific.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q22::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best avoids vague pronouns?{
~A. It helps them with it.#Incorrect. The pronouns are vague.
=B. Extended library hours help students complete assignments after school.#Correct. This names the subject and benefit clearly.
~C. This is good for them.#Incorrect. This is vague.
~D. They need it because it helps.#Incorrect. This uses unclear pronouns.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q23::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is punctuated correctly?{
~A. Extended hours would help students, because they need a place to study.#Incorrect. The comma before because is unnecessary here.
~B. Extended hours would help, students because they need a place to study.#Incorrect. The comma interrupts the sentence.
=C. Extended hours would help students because they need a place to study.#Correct. This is correctly punctuated.
~D. Extended hours, would help students because they need a place to study.#Incorrect. The comma separates subject and verb.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q24::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision best keeps the main idea?{
~A. Change the paragraph to a story about sports.#Incorrect. This changes the topic.
~B. Delete the claim and leave only details.#Incorrect. This weakens the draft.
~C. Add unrelated facts about cafeteria food.#Incorrect. This changes focus.
=D. Keep the library-hours claim and add clearer reasons for school leaders.#Correct. This protects the main idea while improving audience fit.
}

::ENG2_U05_L05_Q25::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which checklist best matches Lesson 5 revision?{
=A. Identify audience, read feedback, choose an action, revise wording or evidence, and explain the improvement.#Correct. This is the Lesson 5 revision process.
~B. Ignore feedback, add random sentences, and submit.#Incorrect. This does not support revision.
~C. Replace the topic with a new one every time.#Incorrect. Revision should usually preserve the main idea.
~D. Use only casual language and no evidence.#Incorrect. Audience needs require clear and appropriate support.
}
